msgid "runtime-preset:list/inspector/description"
msgstr ""
"You can manage settings applied from ExMenu presets.\n\n"
"By pressing the '+' button, you can add a preset object, and the values can be modified from the added object.\n"
"The preset name will be the name of the object.\n"
"You can change the order of presets in the list to adjust the menu order generated in ExMenu."

msgid "runtime-preset:inspector/description"
msgstr ""
"The Preset Editor is a screen for saving and loading settings.\n"
"By changing the settings of this object, you can apply presets from the menu generated in ExMenu.\n\n"
"The preset name will be the name of this object.\n"
"Each function must be enabled in the parent object to be used.\n"
"If the functions are not enabled, selecting this preset will not change the values.\n"
"This is convenient for cases where you want to adjust only specific settings, such as changing colors only."

