## Lighting Settings

msgid "category:lighting/description"
msgstr ""
"Settings related to overall lighting.\n"
"[Brightness Lower Limit] and [Brightness Upper Limit] are the primary features.\n"
"By adjusting these parameters, you can match the brightness to fit the world.\n\n"
"[Monochromize Lighting] is a feature that converts the color of the world light affecting the avatar into monochrome.\n"
"This ensures that the avatar's color remains unchanged while only the brightness is adjusted when exposed to colored light.\n\n"
"[Unlit] is a parameter that disables lighting effects on the avatar.\n"
"Using this feature allows you to control the impact of the world's light on the avatar.\n\n"
"[Emission] is a parameter to adjust the strength of the avatar's emission.\n"
"This prevents excessive brightness in dark areas or overexposure caused by PostProcess effects.\n\n"
"[Light Direction] allows you to override the influence of the light source on the avatar as to which direction it is being illuminated from.\n"
"This allows you to receive light from any direction, regardless of the light source position. It can be turned off at 0%."

msgid "settings:lighting/min-light/label"
msgstr "Brightness Lower Limit"

msgid "settings:lighting/min-light/description"
msgstr ""
"Control Parameter\n"
"lilToon:_LightMinLimit\n"
"poiyomi:_LightingMinLightBrightness\n"
"UnlitWF:_GL_LevelMin"

